      "writtenOn": "2022-06-14T08:05:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the code around e.g. USB_SPI_REQ_ENABLE at the bottom of this file, it is evident that there is no attempt at guarding against multiple host processes simultaneously trying to use the USB-\u003eSPI forwarding.\n\nI think it is reasonable to expect servod or an equivalent host-side process to perform arbitration between multiple processes attempting to use the same SPI controller.  For one thing, only one process can claim the particular USB interface at a time, so whatever process does that would have to forward requests from other processes, which may want to simultaneously perform SPI operations.\n\nGiven the above, I think it is reasonable to have the uServo/HyperDebug firmware we \"dumb\" and not attempt to keep track of multiple host processes passing it requests.",
      "parentUuid": "36da9462_3825bd25",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 347,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 363,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "690d32269160b893c7ff78f1e6634945aec054f3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
